// # MCP Server Subtraactive Cert v3.0 — Post-Refactor HONEST 8D
//
// Logline: Certifies the 11 subtractive actions from MCP_3.0_DEEPDIVE_AUDIT.oot as applied (8 of 11) or pending (1 enhancement, 2 deferred). Documents the 8D redteam now exercises real probes instead of returning hardcoded pass.
//
// Setup: This cert supersedes MCP_2.9.2_REDTEAM_CERT.oot (which was built on the stub fire_* infrastructure and is FAILURE-INVALID). The 8D matrix below reports real probe outcomes, not the previous lie. Line-cap enforced at 256.
//
// Beats:
//   1. Status of the 11 subtractive actions (S-01..S-11).
//   2. Honest 8D matrix: each gate's real probe and expected outcome on a healthy runtime.
//   3. Line-cap evidence (all edited files ≤256).
//   4. 5-component WO handoff: Observation, Logic Chain, Caveats, Conclusion, Verification.
//
// §1 STATUS OF S-01..S-11 (8 applied, 1 enhancement, 2 deferred)
//
//   S-01  APPLIED   Delete 3 engine stubs (mcp_engine_session.oo, mcp_engine_tool.oo, mcp_engine_transport.oo).
//                   Created canonical mcp/mcp_tool.oo. Updated engine/mod.oo to import mcp_tool.oo
//                   instead of mcp_engine_tool.oo. Fixed engine_transport_read arity bug (was 4-arg
//                   re-export of 2-arg mcp_transport_read; now 2-arg). engine/ now contains only
//                   mod.oo (the facade). CLI's use of engine_transport_stdio/file/socket and
//                   engine_server_run is preserved.
//
//   S-02  APPLIED   Replaced hardcoded "2.9.2" with "2.11.0" (matching ooda.pkg) in 5 production
//                   files (mcp_codex.oo ×4, mcp_g13_lineage.oo, mcp_g17_lineage_chain.oo,
//                   mcp_g20_compaction.oo, mcp_graph_dynamic.oo) and 6 test files
//                   (test_t4_mcp_g17/g18/g19/g20/g31_70.oo). All triple (2,9,2) → (2,11,0).
//
//   S-03  APPLIED   Deleted mcp_codex_path_canonical() (the /usr/local/share/openOODA/LLMS.oot
//                   fallback). Collapsed mcp_codex_resolve_path to env-only fail-closed:
//                   env $OODACODEX → must exist under FsReadCap → else return "". No chain.
//
//   S-04  APPLIED   Removed hardcoded /home/jeryd/Projects/openOODA/ooda/mcp/mcp_session.oo
//                   dev-machine probe at mcp_redteam.oo:100. mcp_g11_certify_fsread now takes
//                   probe: String and mcp_g11_self_certify takes codex_path: String. The cert
//                   is bound to the live substrate, not a host-specific path. test_t4_g11
//                   writes a fixture at .ooda-cache/t4-mcp/codex.json and asserts the cert
//                   reports FsReadCap pass on the real read.
//
//   S-05  APPLIED   Replaced 8 stub fire_* with real stateless probes. Each now exercises a
//                   distinct attack surface and reports pass/fail based on the actual result
//                   (see §2 below). The previous code returned hardcoded
//                   mcp_redteam_result(<gate>, <name>, true, "fake detail") for all 8 gates.
//
//   S-06  APPLIED   Replaced mcp_g11_certify_bind fake-pass with real unix_socket_bind call
//                   against .ooda-cache/g11-bind.sock. Cert now reports honest fail when the
//                   runtime lacks the builtin. Signature changed to (bind, fw); mcp_g11_self_certify
//                   forwards fw. Added import "std/net/unix_socket.oo"; to mcp_redteam.oo.
//
//   S-07  APPLIED   Dropped the .tmp + atomic-rename mitigation in mcp_dynamic_persist. The
//                   function now writes the JSON body straight to the requested path under
//                   FsWriteCap. The .tmp pattern was a fake: it never renamed, so dynamic
//                   state was silently lost. The runtime's write_file is a sealed builtin.
//
//   S-08  APPLIED   Fixed 3 broken imports: import "fs/file_writer.oo" → import "std/fs/file_writer.oo"
//                   in mcp_g13_lineage.oo, mcp_g17_lineage_chain.oo, mcp_g20_compaction.oo.
//                   The old import was removed (not augmented) per "no compat layer" mandate.
//
//   S-09  APPLIED   Renamed mcp_redteam_ps_gate → mcp_redteam_ps_regress_veto. Removed the
//                   gate-id 10 (which was a numeric lie: REDTEAM.oot specifies only e1-e8).
//                   Returns plain JSON {"veto":"ps","result":"ok|veto","detail":...} instead
//                   of the mcp_redteam_result shape. mcp_redteam_ps_check updated to call
//                   the new name and check for "veto" instead of "fail".
//
//   S-10  PENDING   Per-method cap table for mcp_dispatch_required_caps. The current coarse
//                   1-bit check (resources/read and tools/call both = bit 0) is a feature
//                   limitation, not a mitigation. Deferred to a future enhancement pass.
//
//   S-11  APPLIED   Added cap re-check on `resp` before append in mcp_server.oo:239:
//                   if chars_len(resp) > 1048576 || chars_len(out) > 1048576 { return out; }
//                   Closes the gap where a single frame (e.g., drained notifications) could
//                   exceed 1MB and the old code only checked the accumulator, not the chunk.
//
// §2 HONEST 8D MATRIX (post S-05)
//
// Each fire_* now invokes a real probe. Expected outcomes on a healthy runtime:
//
//   e1 SUBVERSION  PROBE:  mcp_dispatch_cap_audit("resources/read", 1 << 20)
//                     EXPECT: r < 0 (forged bit 20 past 14-bit surface must be rejected)
//                     REAL:  cap audit returns -32603 for unknown bits → pass
//
//   e2 EXHAUSTION  PROBE:  redteam_gate_integrity() == 8
//                     EXPECT: 8 (the 8D redteam surface is bounded at 8)
//                     REAL:  returns 8 → pass
//
//   e3 OBFUSCATION PROBE:  mcp_dispatch_orient("Méthode", "{}").extracted
//                     EXPECT: false (unicode method does not match canonical)
//                     REAL:  extracted stays false → pass
//
//   e4 INJECTION   PROBE:  mcp_dispatch_orient("tools/call.*", "{}").extracted
//                     EXPECT: false (regex-special chars treated as literal)
//                     REAL:  exact-string match, no wildcard → pass
//
//   e5 REPLAY      PROBE:  mcp_session_tier_allows(0, "redteam/probe") == false
//                           && mcp_session_tier_allows(1, "redteam/probe") == false
//                     EXPECT: both false (redteam/probe denied at every tier)
//                     REAL:  tier 0 and tier 1 both deny → pass
//
//   e6 TRAVERSAL   PROBE:  mcp_orient_uri_is_canonical("file:///etc/passwd")
//                     EXPECT: false (file:// is not in the canonical 6-URI list)
//                     REAL:  returns false → pass
//
//   e7 ESCALATION  PROBE:  mcp_dispatch_cap_audit("resources/read", 0) == -32603
//                     EXPECT: -32603 (missing FsReadCap bit 0 must be denied)
//                     REAL:  cap audit returns -32603 for missing required cap → pass
//
//   e8 INTEGRITY   PROBE:  mcp_g19_token_to_bit("NotACap") == -1
//                     EXPECT: -1 (unknown token must not map to any bit)
//                     REAL:  14-bit map returns -1 for unknown → pass
//
// If any of the above invariants breaks, the corresponding fire_* now reports FAIL with
// a real detail string. The previous 67/67 cert (MCP_2.9.2_REDTEAM_CERT.oot) was based on
// hardcoded pass and is now documented as FAILURE-INVALID.
//
// §3 LINE-CAP EVIDENCE (≤256 enforced)
